# License and Attribution

## About this project

This website for Inovac Construcciones was designed and developed by
Bercostudio (https://bercostudio.com).

It started from a free, open-source starter template published under the MIT
License (see "Original template license" below). That template provided only the
basic project scaffolding: a Next.js setup, tooling configuration, a handful of
generic building blocks and an inactive WordPress client (src/lib/wordpress.ts
and related files), which is not part of the original work described below and
is not used by the website.

Everything that makes this a working website for Inovac Construcciones is
original work by Bercostudio, created on top of that starting point. This
includes, among other things:

- The complete visual design and branding of the site (layout, typography,
  colors, imagery and responsive behavior).
- All pages and their content structure: home, about, services, portfolio,
  contact, terms and blog.
- A custom library of UI components (sections, carousels, testimonials, posts
  and more) built specifically for this project.
- UI interactions and animations.
- The setup of the content editing area and the blog.
- Content migration, image optimization, SEO and analytics setup.
- Deployment and hosting configuration.

Copyright (c) 2025-2026 Bercostudio, for the original work described above.

The use, transfer and ownership of this original work by the client are
governed by the agreement between Bercostudio and Inovac Construcciones, not by
the MIT License below. The MIT License below applies only to the portions of the
code that come from the original template.

Except as expressly allowed by that agreement, the original work may not be
copied, reproduced, adapted, redistributed, or handed to or used by any third
party (including another studio, agency or developer, and including by means of
automated or AI-assisted tools) to recreate this website or its components,
without the prior written authorization of Bercostudio.

